---
import Section from "./Section.astro";

// A low-level view of Cairn's request/data path and its durability contract, grounded in
// the spec (data plane 6–7, metadata 11–12, durability 8–10). No images: hairline tiers +
// mono chips + a one-line note per tier that reflow at every width. Top-to-bottom is flow.
const layers = [
  {
    tier: "Clients",
    nodes: ["S3 SDKs", "aws CLI", "Console", "presigned URLs"],
    desc: "Any unmodified S3 client. Requests are signed with SigV4 or carry a Bearer token; the console drives the same API over its session.",
  },
  {
    tier: "Listeners",
    nodes: [":7373 — S3 data plane", ":7374 — console + /api/v1", "/healthz · /readyz · /metrics", "AWS-STS"],
    desc: "Two ports, one process. Health, metrics and the STS mint answer on :7373 ahead of the concurrency limiter.",
  },
  {
    tier: "Request pipeline",
    nodes: ["authenticate", "authorize — policy · ACL · BPA · ownership", "S3 handler + lifecycle", "chunked decoder", "SSE seal / open"],
    desc: "Each request is authenticated, then run through a real policy-evaluation engine, then handled. Bodies stream; server-side encryption seals on write and opens on read, and fails closed.",
  },
  {
    tier: "Metadata",
    nodes: ["Writer — group-commit", "WAL read pool", "read-through cache", "SQLite (WAL)"],
    desc: "All writes funnel through one group-committing writer — the single linearization point. Reads come off a WAL connection pool; a bounded cache fronts both.",
  },
  {
    tier: "Object bytes",
    nodes: ["BlobStore", "plain files (POSIX)", "block compression", "reconciliation"],
    desc: "Object data is ordinary files on the filesystem. Writes stage, fsync, and rename into place; a bounded reconciliation reclaims orphaned blobs on restart.",
  },
  {
    tier: "Background",
    nodes: ["replication", "lifecycle", "webhooks", "integrity scrub", "multipart sweep", "key re-wrap"],
    desc: "Durable outbox-driven workers run off the metadata store: asynchronous replication, lifecycle expiry, webhook delivery, and an opt-in integrity scrub.",
  },
];

// The write path is an ordered contract: bytes are durable before the metadata
// transaction that references them, and that commit is the one linearization point.
const steps = [
  "stage bytes",
  "fsync file",
  "rename",
  "fsync dir",
  "validate hashes",
  "commit metadata",
  "reclaim",
];
---

<Section eyebrow="Architecture" title="How it works">
  <p>
    Cairn is one process with two listeners and two durable stores — no clustering layer, no external
    database, no separate storage daemon. A request flows straight down the stack: authenticated,
    authorized, and handled, then committed. Reads come off a WAL pool; every write goes through a
    single group-committing writer, so the database has exactly one linearization point. Each store
    sits behind a small trait interface, so the SQLite metadata engine, the file BlobStore, and the
    crypto layer are swappable without touching the S3 surface above them.
  </p>

  <div class="arch">
    {
      layers.map((l, i) => (
        <>
          {i > 0 && <span class="arch__link" aria-hidden="true" />}
          <div class="arch__layer">
            <span class="arch__tier">{l.tier}</span>
            <div class="arch__body">
              <div class="arch__nodes">
                {l.nodes.map((n) => (
                  <span class="chip">{n}</span>
                ))}
              </div>
              <p class="arch__desc">{l.desc}</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </>
      ))
    }
  </div>

  <p class="arch__lead">
    Durability is an ordered contract. Object bytes are staged and fsynced <em>before</em> the
    metadata transaction that references them, and that commit is the single point where a write
    becomes real — so an acknowledged write has already survived power loss. On restart, Cairn
    reconciles and reclaims anything a crash left behind.
  </p>

  <div class="writepath" role="list" aria-label="Durable write path, in order">
    {
      steps.map((s, i) => (
        <>
          {i > 0 && (
            <span class="writepath__arrow" aria-hidden="true">
              →
            </span>
          )}
          <span role="listitem" class="writepath__step">
            <span class="writepath__n">{i + 1}</span>
            {s}
          </span>
        </>
      ))
    }
  </div>
  <p class="writepath__note">
    The metadata commit (step 6) is the linearization point: nothing before it is acknowledged, and
    nothing after it can lose the object.
  </p>
</Section>

<style>
  /* --- Layered flow diagram: each tier is a full-width hairline row, so it reflows
         cleanly and never scrolls sideways. Top-to-bottom implies the request flow. --- */
  .arch {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }
  .arch__layer {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 8rem 1fr;
    gap: 0.5rem 0.9rem;
    align-items: start;
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 0.8rem 0.9rem;
    background: var(--bg-subtle);
  }
  .arch__tier {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    color: var(--fg-faint);
    padding-top: 0.3rem;
  }
  .arch__nodes {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }
  .chip {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline-bold);
    border-radius: 5px;
    padding: 0.25rem 0.55rem;
  }
  .arch__desc {
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    margin-top: 0.55rem;
    max-width: 52ch;
  }
  /* A centered hairline between tiers, in the page's own 1px-rule language. */
  .arch__link {
    width: 1px;
    height: var(--space-4);
    margin-inline: auto;
    background: var(--hairline-bold);
  }

  /* --- The durable write path: an ordered row of numbered steps that wraps instead
         of scrolling. The arrows are flow, not content (aria-hidden). --- */
  .arch__lead {
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
  }
  .writepath {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.45rem 0.35rem;
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
  }
  .writepath__step {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.55ch;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 0.3rem 0.6rem;
  }
  .writepath__n {
    font-size: 0.74em;
    color: var(--fg-faint);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .writepath__arrow {
    color: var(--fg-faint);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
  }
  .writepath__note {
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--fg-faint);
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
  }

  /* Narrow screens: tier label stacks above its nodes; chips wrap. No horizontal scroll. */
  @media (max-width: 34rem) {
    .arch__layer {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .arch__tier {
      padding-top: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
